WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:06.000
We saw how we can grant a user or group&nbsp;
specific access to a part of a database&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.420
in the previous video. Let's look further into&nbsp;
some granting options. Here is one scenario:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:18.480
an administrator may want to save time in overall&nbsp;
database administration through not only granting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:24.960
a role to someone, but also giving that person,&nbsp;
or sometimes group, the option to grant the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:31.860
permission to others. I have a blank query window&nbsp;
open and I'm going to type a GRANT statement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:40.980
explain it, and then execute it. I will type&nbsp;
GRANT EXECUTE ON GetDepartment to procTester&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:48.540
WITH GRANT OPTION. Before I run this statement,&nbsp;
let's go through its details. GRANT grants a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:55.140
privilege, in this case Execute, on an object.&nbsp;
The object, in this example, GetDepartment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.140 --> 00:01:01.920
is a stored procedure, which we will detail later&nbsp;
in this course. procTester is a user account that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:07.200
I added to this SQL Server instance and then to&nbsp;
this database. The WITH GRANT OPTION clause gives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:14.280
this account, procTester, the ability to grant&nbsp;
execute privileges on this stored procedure to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.660
other users and groups. While this grant is a&nbsp;
convenience for allowing people to help control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:24.900
access to an object, of course administrators&nbsp;
need to show discretion as to who they grant these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:31.020
options to when granting permissions on a resource&nbsp;
as we want to make sure, as we execute this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:36.840
only those who know how to handle permissions&nbsp;
properly grant permissions to others.

